==Strategy==
There's a few ways to go about tackling this stage: for one, if you have [[Meditation Cat (Special Cat)|Paragon Cat]], you can effectively ignore its gimmick entirely so long as you keep the Diabrollows at a good distance, netting you a free win. Otherwise, you want to quickly clear out the flock of Brollow variants with many high DPH attackers like [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] and [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train Cat]]. Wave Shields like [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Octopus Cat]] are crucial in keeping [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jelly Dumpling]]/Paragon Cat alive while retaining ground. To deal with Big Sal, you can simply elect to kill him with [[Teacher BearCat (Rare Cat)|Cadaver BearCats]] + the [[Ototo Corps#Holy Blast|Holy Blast]], or perpetually stall him with [[Welterweight Cat (Rare Cat)|Ol' Reliable]], either works.

It is borderline impossible to rush the stage with melee units due to the prescence of Zollows that consistently clear out everything at the enemy base. You have no other option but to wait out their migration.

